Typed Structured Data Hashing and Signing
	•	Standard for signing structured, human-readable messages off-chain.
	•	Instead of signing a raw transaction (binary blob), users sign typed data with clear fields.

Example use cases:
	•	Permit approvals (EIP-2612): sign a message to allow spending tokens, without sending an on-chain approval tx.
	•	Meta-transactions: user signs an intent, a relayer submits it on-chain.
	•	Off-chain agreements: swaps, orders, settlements — validated on-chain later.

Benefits:
	•	Prevents phishing & replay attacks (domain separator + nonce).
	•	Messages are human-readable (wallet shows “You allow 100 DAI to be spent by 0x…”).
	•	Decouples signing from execution → gasless UX, batch transactions, Validium off-chain intents (like in your setup).

